# One who [[pitch]]es anything, as [[hay]], [[quoit]]s, a [[ball]], etc.
# {{lb|en|baseball|softball}} The [[player]] who delivers the ball to the [[batter]].
# {{lb|en|slang}} A [[drug dealer]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2000|author=Michael Massing|title=The Fix|page=67
|passage=To the residents of Spanish Harlem, these '''pitchers''' embodied the drug trade at its most sinister; they were the dealers and pushers who were destroying their neighborhood.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete|UK|slang}} One who puts [[counterfeit]] [[money]] into [[circulation]].
#: {{syn|en|snide pitcher}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1863|author=Blanchard Jerrold|title=Signals of Distress in Refuges and Homes of Charity (etc.)|page=2
|passage=To discover {{...}} how the honest poor are compelled to hob-and-nob with the “[[shoful]] '''pitcher'''” and the “gun,” it is necessary to visit the vast nursery-grounds of crime.}}
# {{lb|en|chiefly|US|colloquial}} The [[top]] partner in a [[homosexual]] [[relationship]] or penetrator in a [[sexual]] [[encounter]] between two men.
#: {{syn|en|top}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A sort of [[crowbar]] for [[dig]]ging.
# One who makes a pitch or proposal.
#: {{ux|en|The '''pitcher''' of the new film stands to earn millions.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete|UK|slang}} A person who sells anything in the streets.

